<TABLE border=0 cellpadding=0 cellspacing=0>
	<TR>
		<TD align=center><FONT face=verdana size=1 color=#ff4500><B>Policies/Guidelines</B></FONT></TD>
	</TR>

		<TR>
			<TD align=center><FONT face=verdana size=1 color=#ff4500>Last Altered - 5/2/2001 4:58:32 PM</FONT></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b>Guidelines of Conduct</b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>Your actions reflect on all others who wear the tag of the Clan Stormbringer</p>
<p>As a guild, the Clan Stormbringer acknowledges the published "Play Nice Policies" of Verant as the basic guideline for the conduct of the members of the guild.</p>
<p>A member of the Clan should always respect another player's character. Name-calling and other disparaging remarks towards another bring no honor upon oneself. If you do have a serious problem with another player, it is appropriate to bring this to the attention of the officers of the guild. 
It's important to remember that the services of another guild member are not owed to you. Remember the other guild members are here to play too. Its unfair to expect them to drop everything and help you, they may have a commitment to their current group. Please remember, when you ask -- you are asking for a favor and that player has a right to say no.</p>
<p>A Clan member's word is their honor, in any world. If you tell a guild member, or anyone for that matter, that you will assist them. Do it. Respect their time in this world, once you give your word to assist them -- get there. Do as you said you would. Uphold your word, it is one of the most valuable things here.</p>







</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b>Expectations of Participation</b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>The participation of its members is vital to the survival of the guild. Loyalty and Commitment are core values and the guild feels that these values reflect themselves in participation in guild events. </p>
<p>Clan Stormbringer has the expectation that a member will participate in approximately 40% of the events the guild stages. Failure to maintain this level of participation can result in a member's status being set to inactive. The guild's Chancellor on a quarterly basis will assess level of participation for the membership.</p>
<p>In addition to meeting the requirements for membership, players are expected to maintain current information on their guilded characters on the guild's website. Failure to maintain current information may lead to a player's status to be set to inactive.</p>

</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b>Violations </b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p><ul><li>Harassment. Overt and unwanted communication of a sexual nature. No dirty talk if there is any chance of offending someone.</li>
<li>Excessive Begging The Clan Stormbringer are a very generous and giving group of players. Abuse of this generosity through excessive requests for items, platinum or services is grounds for a legitimate complaint that could lead to a player's removal from the guild.</li>
<li>Kill Stealing. If an area or spawn is being camped please respect the priority of those players. If an area has been broken and is under the control of another group, respect their rights to exploit their efforts.
Scams. Trying to cheat another player or the game.</li>
<li>Intentional Training. This will get you banned from the game. If a situation develops where you are not having fun then leave that zone and go somewhere you will.</li></ul></p>

</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD>&nbsp;</TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><b>Removal From the Guild</b></TD>
		</TR>
		<TR>
			<TD align=left><FONT face=verdana size=2 color='black'><p>A player may be removed from the guild under the following circumstances.</p>
<p>Administrative Removal
A player may be removed from the roster of the Clan Stormbringer upon the request of the player.
A player may be removed from the roster of the Clan Stormbringer when their guild status has remained inactive for 2 quarters.</p>
<p>Disciplinary Removal
If a player consistently and willfully behaves in a manner that is contrary to the spirit of the guidelines of the charter of the Clan Stormbringer they may be removed from the guild. To be removed, a player must have a formal grievance filed against them. Grievances may be filed via e-mail. The grievance must supply sufficient detail for verification. A player with a grievance will be notified of the grievance within 7 days of the original receipt. The player will be informed of the nature of the complaint and the identity of the player filing the grievance. The Guild Chancellor will attempt determine the facts and present his findings to the guild officers. If 75% of the officers with an active status concur, the player will be removed from the guild.
Guild officers, including the leader, are not exempt from grievances. </p>



</TD>
		</TR>
